# PMI surface reactions for the DIII-D boron source hitting a carbon wall.
# Pair this with an HDF5 table whose coefficients match boron-on-carbon
# impacts if you want the reflection/sputtering probabilities to be
# physically consistent with the emitted species.
#
# Reaction roles in this file:
#   R = reflected boron (neutralized on impact)
#   S = sputtered carbon from the substrate
#   A = absorbed/implanted boron
#
# Only boron impact species are defined here, since the active emitted
# mixture is boronSource. If you later turn carbonSource back on, use a
# separate PMI model/table for carbon impacts instead of reusing boron
# coefficients for both species.

B --> B
R Simple 1.0

B --> C
S Simple 1.0

B --> NULL
A Simple 1.0

B+ --> B
R Simple 1.0

B+ --> C
S Simple 1.0

B+ --> NULL
A Simple 1.0

B2+ --> B
R Simple 1.0

B2+ --> C
S Simple 1.0

B2+ --> NULL
A Simple 1.0

B3+ --> B
R Simple 1.0

B3+ --> C
S Simple 1.0

B3+ --> NULL
A Simple 1.0

B4+ --> B
R Simple 1.0

B4+ --> C
S Simple 1.0

B4+ --> NULL
A Simple 1.0

B5+ --> B
R Simple 1.0

B5+ --> C
S Simple 1.0

B5+ --> NULL
A Simple 1.0


